# Third party content

## tau2-bench banking knowledge domain

`data/tau2/banking_knowledge/` is vendored from **tau2-bench** by Sierra Research,
used under the MIT License.

    Source:  https://github.com/sierra-research/tau2-bench
    License: MIT, reproduced verbatim with its own copyright line in
             data/tau2/LICENSE
    Files:   717 tracked -- 698 knowledge documents, tasks.json (97
             customer service tasks), db.json, and 17 prompt files

The documents and the `required_documents` list on each task are reproduced
unmodified. That list is what this repository uses as its retrieval gold set, which
is the point of vendoring it: the correct answer to every question here was fixed by
somebody outside this project, before this project ran. Nothing in `src/` or `evals/`
edits these files, and no check regenerates them.

`tasks_voice.json` is excluded from version control for size; nothing in this
repository reads it.

## Langfuse compose file

`deploy/docker-compose.yml` is adapted from the compose file **Langfuse GmbH** publishes for
running Langfuse yourself, used under the MIT License.

    Source:  https://github.com/langfuse/langfuse
    License: MIT, reproduced verbatim with its own copyright line in
             deploy/LICENSE.langfuse

Most of it is upstream's, verbatim: the six services, both YAML anchors and the bulk of the
environment. The changes here are narrow and are about keeping it off the network -- four
published ports removed, two bound to 127.0.0.1, a healthcheck added to langfuse-web, and
the LANGFUSE_INIT_* values filled in with obviously fake development credentials.

Copyright for the vendored tau2-bench content remains with the tau2-bench authors, and for
the compose file with Langfuse GmbH. Everything else in this repository is covered by the
MIT License in `LICENSE`.

Naming the holders here is not on its own enough, which is why the two files above exist.
The MIT License requires that "the above copyright notice and this permission notice"
travel with any substantial portion of the software, and a prose sentence in a NOTICE is
neither of those things: it names a holder without reproducing the grant or the warranty
disclaimer either of them made. It also does not survive the reading that matters, which
is a machine's -- with one unscoped `LICENSE` at the root and nothing beside the vendored
trees, GitHub's sidebar and the usual scanners resolve all 717 tau2 files and the compose
file to this repository's own copyright line.
